msgid "External LEDs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:7
#: 63356fc6bb5c40d1a4a29e05e1c6a7d1
msgid "An external LED or LED Display can be added by connecting it to the autopilot's I2C port or, in 4.0 and later versions, if a serially programmed device, via an output using the SERVOx_FUNCTION for that output. DroneCAN LEDs on the CANBUS are also supported (See :ref:`DroneCAN Setup <common-uavcan-setup-advanced>` )."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:10
#: 01780806e8d24b609bde63929da83b76
msgid "Note that the same grouping restrictions which apply to setting outputs to different PWM rates and/or DShot, apply to LEDs also since the timer associated with each group of outputs cannot be used for different rates. See also  :ref:`Mixing ESC Protocols<mixing-escs>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:13
#: 497475a1edf343b3bdd22c1503e5a79a
msgid "RGB LEDs/Displays with I2C Connection"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:15
#: 430365d2212e4afca3485365125c761f
msgid "Two types of I2C devices are supported: I2C connected RGB LEDS using an LED driver chip and OLED displays."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:17
#: 78d0f47aabf247c890c307c4dd243acf
msgid "RGB LEDs/drivers supported are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:19
#: 821d659a337f410d9e6b899cce988bd1
msgid "Toshiba LEDs (no longer manufactured)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:20
#: c74481c7d86a4bd593ee8fd9841c0bdf
msgid "PCA9685 driver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:21
#: f215daf761de4346b65ecd7c0f8c6143
msgid "NCP5623 driver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:23
#: da426441c75649a389fea5da3ce303e5
msgid "OLED Displays supported are SSH1106 and SSD1306 with 128x64 pixel displays. See :ref:`common-display-onboard` for more information."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:29
#: d8da6dde5f0d4cfd8571b6742c334e8a
msgid "Because most users use an external :ref:`GPS and Compass module <common-positioning-landing-page>`, an I2C splitter is recommended, such as shown below. The :ref:`NTF_LED_TYPES<NTF_LED_TYPES>` parameter should be set to the controller type used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:35
#: 6b2e6cbc779342cc86bebe5505c19bde
msgid "Serially Connected Devices"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:37
#: 2b0bc42274734933b22b1d93a1a28bae
msgid "Serial LEDs connected to an output require that the output be DMA capable for proper operation. If the output is DShot capable, then its DMA capable. Check the autopilot's documentation to determine if the output is DShot capable,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:39
#: 4c2252e54d7d4da2bf9e2894cf0543c6
msgid "Currently, ArduPilot supports Neopixel and ProfiLED RGB LED strings on the autopilot's output using ``SERVOx_FUNCTION`` 120 thru 123. They can be used for NTF notifications from the autopilot on status and warnings like other RGB LEDs, or be programmed in unlimited ways using LUA scripts on the autopilot's SD card. For use with scripting the output function must be set to a scripting output function (94 - 109) the script then assigns this output to LEDs. See :ref:`common-lua-scripts` for more use examples using LUA scripts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:43
#: 730b2e96dde2479ea0a3646ccfae6b6a
msgid "Serial LEDs require a whole pwm group, more information about your autopilot's PWM groups can be found on it's :ref:`hardware page<common-autopilots>`. To check that the desired outputs have been setup correctly look for the PWM types message in your GCS's messages tab. See :ref:`common-gpios`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:51
#: f8ffb3bb744a4c539dda4d81a37e496e
msgid "Be sure the output is configures as normal PWM instead of a GPIO output. Flight controllers with a IOMCU can only use the AUX outputs for connecting serial LEDs. To check that the desired outputs have been setup correctly look for the PWM types message in your GCS's messages tab. See :ref:`common-gpios`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:54
#: dc55ad3a72f445128b726cecb3dcd0c9
msgid "PWM Connected Strobes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:56
#: 2f17f1fb558c4a66aa931c6bd77747fd
msgid "High-intensity strobes often connect to standard servo outputs and are controlled via PWM (RC pass-through) or specific LED functions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:70
#: 526f3c2a356a4df0bffbe8f9fff517c7
msgid "NTF LED Meaning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:72
#: 3027969116ce428fa21945a878fcd286
msgid "The meaning of the colors and flash patterns are shown in :ref:`common-leds-pixhawk` if the ``standard`` default protocol is set for :ref:`NTF_LED_OVERRIDE<NTF_LED_OVERRIDE>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-external-leds.rst:74
#: a413ab991d1f4950b17491067497c099
msgid "The brightness and number of LEDs can be controlled by modifying the :ref:`NTF_LED_BRIGHT <NTF_LED_BRIGHT>` and :ref:`NTF_LED_LEN <NTF_LED_LEN>`"
msgstr ""
